  "result": "Geomycin, II. Mitteil.; Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXIX. Mitteil. (https://openalex.org/W2072810484)\nciteturn40search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 72.1 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # Geomycin, II. ... DOI: 10.1002/cber.19540871128 ...   * Hans Brockmann — University of Göttingen (ROR)\n# Geomycin, II. Mitteil.; Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXIX. Mitteil.\n\nOpenAlex ID: W2072810484\n\nDOI: 10.1002/cber.19540871128\n\nType: article\n\nYear: 1954\n\nPublication date: 1954-11-01\n\nLanguage: de\n\n## Source\n\nName: Chemische Berichte\n\nISSN-L: 0009-2940\n\nISSN: 0009-2940\n\nPublisher: Wiley\n\n## Citation\n\nVolume: 87\n\nIssue: 11\n\nPages: 1779–1799\n\n## Article links\n\n  * Article website\n\n## Authors\n\n  * Hans Brockmann — University of Göttingen (ROR)\n  * Hans Musso — University of Göttingen (ROR)\n\n## Abstract\n\nAbstract Aus Mycel und Kulturlösung von Streptomyces xanthophaeus (nov. spec.) wurde ein neues, gegen grampositive und ‐negative Bakterien wirksames, wasserlösliches Antibioticum, das Geomycin, als kristallisiertes Salz der 4′‐Dimethylamino‐azobenzol‐sulfonsäure‐(4) Im folgenden kurz als Helianthinsalz bezeichnet. isoliert. Geomycin besteht wie Neomycin, Streptothricin und andere basische Antibiotica aus mehreren, einander sehr ähnlichen Komponenten (Geomycin A, B, C und D), die sich papierchromatographisch trennen lassen. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGeomycin, II. Mitteil.; Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXIX. Mitteil. (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/230540556_Geomycin_II_Mitteil_Antibiotica_aus_Actinomyceten_XXIX_Mitteil)\nciteturn40search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; # Geomycin, II. ... DOI:10.1002/cber.19540871128 ... Aus Mycel und Kulturlösung von Streptomyces xanthophaeus (nov. spec.) wurde ein neues, gegen grampositive und ‐negative Bakterien wirksames, wasserlösliches Antibioticum, das Geomycin, als kristallisiertes Salz der 4′‐Dimethylamino‐azobenzol‐sulfonsäure‐(4)Im folgenden kurz als Helianthinsalz bezeichnet. isoliert. ... Pertinent literature about the producer strains were searched using SciFinder software program and it was found that S. xanthophaeus is known to produce diverse array of metabolites including Postproline endopeptidase, Benarthin, β-galactosidaseinhibiting isoflavonoids and geomycins (Brockmann and Musso, 1954;Hazato et al., 1979;Aoyagi et al., 1992;Shibamoto et al., 1993).\n\n# Geomycin, II. Mitteil.; Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXIX. Mitteil.\n\n  * January 2006\n  * Chemische Berichte 87(11):1779-1799\n\nDOI:10.1002/cber.19540871128\n\nAuthors:\n\nHans Brockmann\n\nHans Brockmann\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nHans Musso\n\nHans Musso\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\n## Abstract\n\nAus Mycel und Kulturlösung von Streptomyces xanthophaeus (nov. spec.) wurde ein neues, gegen grampositive und ‐negative Bakterien wirksames, wasserlösliches Antibioticum, das Geomycin, als kristallisiertes Salz der 4′‐Dimethylamino‐azobenzol‐sulfonsäure‐(4)Im folgenden kurz als Helianthinsalz bezeichnet. isoliert. Geomycin besteht wie Neomycin, Streptothricin und andere basische Antibiotica aus mehreren, einander sehr ähnlichen Komponenten (Geomycin A, B, C und D), die sich papierchromatographisch trennen lassen. Die Geomycine sind mehrsäurige Basen, für die als vorläufige Bruttoformel (C6H12O2N2)8–10 angenommen wird.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTHE JOURNAL OF ANTIBIOTICS, SER. A 10(5): 181-188 (1957) (https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/antibioticsa/10/5/10_181/_pdf)\nciteturn40search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.6 years ago; Geomycin reported by BROCKMANN and others7l is also dextrorotatory. ... Chemical studies on antibiotic substances. ... Antibiotics, 5, 343, 1952. ... Geomycin II.\nSummary \nAn antibiotic was isolated from a streptomyces which was assigned to a new \nspecies S. kanamyceticus, n. sp. 0KAMI et UMEZAWA. \nThe antibiotic was obtained by \nthe cation exchange resin process and crystallized as its reineckate. The hydrochlo-\nride of this antibiotic gave positive ninhydrin and the specific rotation was+ 103°. \nThe negative glucosamine test differentiated this antibiotic from fradiomycins (neo-\nmycins B and C) and catenulin. Paperchromatography with 2 % p-toluene sulfonic \nacid in water-saturated butanol differentiated this antibiotic from neamine. \nThe re-\nlative bacteriostatic activities against K. pneumoniae (by the dilution method) and B. \nsubtilis (by the cylinder plate method) differentiated this antibiotic from neamine, \nneomycins B and C. This antibiotic was named kanamycin. It showed the inhibition \nagainst both Gram positive and negative bacteria and it did not show the delayed \ntoxicity. LDo to mice by the intravenous injection was larger than 150 mg/kg. \nReferences \n1) \nUMEZAWA, H., HAYANO, S., & OGATA, Y.: \nClassiffication of antibiotic strains of strepto-\nmyces and their antibiotic substances on the basis of their antibacterial spectra. Jap. Med. J., \n1, 504, 1948. \n2) \nUMEZAWA, H., TAKEUCHI, T., & KUROST.J, E.: Studies on the streptothricin group substan-\nces. \nOn streptothricin A and streptothricin B. Jap, Med. J., 1, 9, 1949. \n3) ISHIDA, N.: \nOn a basic antibiotic of the strain 0-26 closely related to Streptomyces roseoch-\nromogenus. J. Antibiotics, 3, 843, 1950 \n4) WAKSMAN, S.A. & LECHEVALIER, H.A.: \nA neomycin, a new antibiotic against streptomycin-\nresisistant bacteria, including tuberculosis organisms. Science, 109, 305, 1949. \n5) \nMAEDA, K. : \nChemical studies on antibiotic substances. II. On streptothricin BI and Bil. \nJ. Antibiotics, 5, 343, 1952. \n6) DAVISSON, J. W., SOLOMONS, I. A., & LEES, T.M.: \nCatenulin, a new antibiotic. Antibiot. \n& Chemoth., 2, 460, 1952. \n7) \nBROCKMANN, H. & RUSSO, H.: \nGeomycin II. \nChem. Ber., 87, 1779, 1954.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIsolation, Screening, and Identification of Novel Isolates of Actinomycetes from India for Antimicrobial Applications (https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/microbiology/articles/10.3389/fmicb.2016.01921/full)\nciteturn40search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.9 years ago; Crawled: last month; Brockmann H.Musso H. ... Geomycin 2. ... Studies on the biosynthesis of the antibiotic reductiomycin in Streptomyces xanthochromogenus.\n  * 6\n\nBrockmann H.Musso H. (1954). Antibiotics from actinomycetes. XXIX. Geomycin 2. Chem. Ber.87, 1779–1799. 10.1002/cber.19540871128\n\n    * CrossRef\n    * Google Scholar\n    * View reference in article\n\n  * 7\n\nCho H.Beale J. M.Graff C.Mocek U.Nakagawa A.Omura S.et al. (1993). Studies on the biosynthesis of the antibiotic reductiomycin in Streptomyces xanthochromogenus. J. Am. Chem. Soc.115, 12296–12304. 10.1021/ja00079a009\n\n    * CrossRef\n    * Google Scholar\n    * View reference in article\n\n  * 8\n\nGriffiths P. J. F.Ellis G. P. (1972). Benzopyrones—VI1: the ultraviolet absorption spectra of chromone and 2-substituted chromones. Spectrochim. Acta A Mol. Spectros.28, 707–713. 10.1016/0584-8539(72)80039-4\n\n    * CrossRef\n    * Google Scholar\n    * View reference in article\n\n  * 9\n\nHayakawa M. (2008). Studies on the isolation and distribution of rare actinomycetes in soil. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHydrolytischer Abbau der Geomycine; Geomycin, III. Mitteil.: Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXX. Mitteil (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/230540548_Hydrolytischer_Abbau_der_Geomycine_Geomycin_III_Mitteil_Antibiotica_aus_Actinomyceten_XXX_Mitteil)\nciteturn40search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; DOI:10.1002/cber.19550880510 ... Hans Brockmann ... Separatory determination of β-lysine and roseonine, formed by acid hydrolysis of racemomycin-B, an antibiotic produced by a mutant strain of Streptomyces racemochromogenus, was attempted and separation of carbon dioxide, β-lysine (I), and roseonine (II) was effected. ... Since this ratio is different from that of roseothrlcin or geomycin, the antibiotics of the streptothricin series, racemomycin-B was assumed to be a new antibiotic different from these substances.\n\nArticle\n\n# Hydrolytischer Abbau der Geomycine; Geomycin, III. Mitteil.: Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXX. Mitteil\n\n  * January 2006\n  * Chemische Berichte 88(5):648-661\n\nDOI:10.1002/cber.19550880510\n\nAuthors:\n\nHans Brockmann\n\nHans Brockmann\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nHans Musso\n\nHans Musso\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\n## Abstract\n\nBei der Säurehydrolyse des Geomycins entstehen neben Ammoniak und Kohlendioxyd zwei basische Abbauprodukte, die als kristallisierte Salze isoliert wurden. Das eine ließ sich als L‐β‐Lysin identifizieren, das andere, Geamin genannt, ist eine Aminosäure C6H12O3N4, die offenbar einen Amino‐imidazolinring enthält.\n\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHydrolytischer Abbau der Geomycine; Geomycin, III. Mitteil.: Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXX. Mitteil (https://chemistry-europe.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/cber.19550880510)\nciteturn40search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 71.6 years ago; Crawled: last month; # Hydrolytischer Abbau der Geomycine; Geomycin, III. ... Chemistry 114, 515 [1936].\n\nVolume 88, Issue 5 pp. 648-661\n\nArticle\n\n# Hydrolytischer Abbau der Geomycine; Geomycin, III. Mitteil.: Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXX. Mitteil\n\nHans Brockmann, \n\nHans Brockmann\n\nOrganisch-Chemischen Institut der Universität Göttingen\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nHans Musso, \n\nHans Musso\n\nOrganisch-Chemischen Institut der Universität Göttingen\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nHans Brockmann, \n\nHans Brockmann\n\nOrganisch-Chemischen Institut der Universität Göttingen\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nHans Musso, \n\nHans Musso\n\nOrganisch-Chemischen Institut der Universität Göttingen\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nFirst published: Mai 1955\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/cber.19550880510Digital Object Identifier (DOI)\n\n### Abstract\n\nBei der Säurehydrolyse des Geomycins entstehen neben Ammoniak und Kohlendioxyd zwei basische Abbauprodukte, die als kristallisierte Salze isoliert wurden. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVOL. XXV NO. 9  THE JOURNAL OF ANTIBIOTICS  507 (https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/antibiotics1968/25/9/25_9_501/_pdf)\nciteturn40search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.7 years ago; Crawled: 19.0 years ago; 9  THE JOURNAL OF ANTIBIOTICS  507 ... Ten mg of streptolidyl gulosaminide hydrochloride (Rf 0.35 in System 1, 0.22 in System 2, 0.23 in System 3) were obtained; mp 220°C (decomp.). ... N-guan-Streptolidyl gulosaminide sulfate** ... 4) Brockmann, H. ... Musso: Hydrolytischer Abbau der Geomycin; Geomycin. II.\n\nThe fractions 129~137 were evaporated to dryness and then the residue dissolved in 5 ml of water was passed through Dowex 1×8 (Cl⁻). Water was evaporated and residue was dried under reduced pressure to give 5 mg streptolidyl gulosaminide hydrochloride.\n\n**12. N-guan-Streptolidyl gulosaminide sulfate**\n\nThe aqueous solution of streptolidyl gulosaminide hydrochloride was passed through a column of Amberlite IRA-400 (SO₄⁻). Water eluate was concentrated and streptolidyl gulosaminide was precipitated with methanol. The fine precipitate was centrifugated, washed with methanol and then dried over P₂O₅.\n\n**13.** The IR-spectrum (KBr) was measured on a Model UR-10-spectrophotometer\n\n**References**\n\n1) Waksman, S.A. & H.B. Woodruff: Streptothricin, a new selective, bacteriostatic and bactericidal agent, particularly active against gram-negative bacteria. Proc. Soc. Exp. Biol. Med. 49: 207~209, 1942  \n2) Khokhlov, A. S.; M. M. Shemyakin & P. D. Reshetov: Streptothricins. XV. in the book M. M. Shemyakin, A. S. Khokhlov, M. N. Kolosov, L. D. Bergelson & V. K. Antonov: Chimija antibiotikov, Moscow, 1961, p. 1200  \n3) Carter, H. E.; R. K. Clark, Jr., P. Kohn, J. W. Rothrock, W. R. Taylor, C. A. West, G. B. Whitfield & W. G. Jackson: Streptothricin. I. Preparation, properties and hydrolysis products. J. Amer. Chem. Soc. 76: 566~569, 1954  \n4) Brockmann, H. & H. Musso: Hydrolytischer Abbau der Geomycin; Geomycin. II. Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXX. Chem. Ber. 88: 648~661, 1955--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGeomycin IV.; Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten, XLII (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/230540531_Geomycin_IV_Antibiotica_aus_Actinomyceten_XLII)\nciteturn40search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; DOI:10.1002/cber.19590920114 ... Hans Brockmann ... Geomycin, II. ... Aus Mycel und Kulturlösung von Streptomyces xanthophaeus (nov. spec.) wurde ein neues, gegen grampositive und ‐negative Bakterien wirksames, wasserlösliches Antibioticum, das Geomycin, als kristallisiertes Salz der 4′‐Dimethylamino‐azobenzol‐sulfonsäure‐(4)Im folgenden kurz als Helianthinsalz bezeichnet. isoliert.\n\nArticle\n\n# Geomycin IV.; Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten, XLII\n\n  * January 2006\n  * Chemische Berichte 92(1):114-130\n\nDOI:10.1002/cber.19590920114\n\nAuthors:\n\nHans Brockmann\n\nHans Brockmann\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nReimer Cölln\n\nReimer Cölln\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\n## Abstract\n\nIm Geomycin sind vier β‐Lysin‐Reste über ihre ϵ‐Aminogruppe säureamidartig miteinander verbunden. Geamin wird bereits unter sehr milden Bedingungen hydrolytisch abgespalten und ist wahrscheinlich über seine Hydroxygruppe mit dem Teil der Geomycin‐Molekel verknüpft, der bei Partialhydrolyse reduzierende Abbauprodukte liefert und wahrscheinlich Zucker‐ bzw. Aminozucker enthält.\n\nImage: ResearchGate Logo\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStreptomyces xanthophaeus (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Streptomyces_xanthophaeus)\nciteturn40search14 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Streptomyces xanthophaeus produces geomycin, arginylthreonine and diadzein. ... * Brockmann, Hans; Musso, Hans (November 1954). \"Geomycin, II. ... 87 (11): 1779–1799. doi:10.1002/cber.19540871128.\n\n* Brockmann, Hans; Musso, Hans (November 1954). \"Geomycin, II. Mitteil.; Antibiotica aus Actinomyceten. XXIX. Mitteil\". Chemische Berichte. 87 (11): 1779–1799. doi:10.1002/cber.19540871128. \n* J. B., Harborne; T. J., Mabry (1982). The Flavonoids Advances in Research. Boston, MA: Springer US. ISBN 1-4899-2915-0. \n* Florkin, Marcel; Mason, Howard S., eds. (1963). Comparative Biochemistry V5 A Comprehensive Treatise. Burlington: Elsevier Science. ISBN 0-323-14378-4. {{cite book}}: ISBN / Date incompatibility (help) \n* Garrity, George M., ed. (2012). Bergey's manual of systematic bacteriology (2nd ed.). New York: Springer Science + Business Media. ISBN 978-0-387-68233-4. \n* Walter, Karrer (1958). Konstitution und Vorkommen der organischen Pflanzenstoffe exclusive Alkaloide. Basel: Springer Basel. ISBN 3-0348-6808-1. {{cite book}}: ISBN / Date incompatibility (help) \n* Goodfellow, M.; Williams, S. T.; Mordarski, M., eds. (1988). Actinomycetes in Biotechnology. Oxford: Elsevier Science. ISBN 0-08-098433-9. \n* Wagman, Gerald H.; Cooper, Raymond, eds. (1989). Natural products isolation separation methods for antimicrobials, antivirals, and enzyme inhibitors. Amsterdam: Elsevier. ISBN 0-08-085848-1.\n## External links\n\n* Type strain of Streptomyces xanthophaeus at BacDive - the Bacterial Diversity Metadatabase\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nÜber Hans Musso (1925–1988) und sein wissenschaftliches Werk (https://chemistry-europe.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/cber.19921250202)\nciteturn40search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 34.8 years ago; Crawled: last month; M.: Geomycin, ein neues, gegen gramnegative Bakterien wirksames Antibioticum, Naturwissenschaften 1954, 41, 451. ... M.: Geomycin, II.\n\nVolume 125, Issue 2 pp. I-XXIV\n\nArticle\n\n# Über Hans Musso (1925–1988) und sein wissenschaftliches Werk\n\nHenning Hopf, \n\nHenning Hopf\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nHenning Hopf, \n\nHenning Hopf\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nFirst published: February 1992\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/cber.19921250202Digital Object Identifier (DOI)\n\nImage: First page image\n\n## References\n\n  * 1 H. Brockmann, H. M.: Die papierchromatographische Trennung von Glycinpeptiden, Naturwissenschaften 1951, 38, 11.\n\nCAS Google Scholar\n\n  * 2 H. Brockmann, H. M.: Zur Synthese höhermolekularer Polypeptide, Naturwissenschaften 1953, 40, 553.\n\nCAS Web of Science® Google Scholar\n\n  * 3 H. Brockmann, H. M.: Geomycin, ein neues, gegen gramnegative Bakterien wirksames Antibioticum, Naturwissenschaften 1954, 41, 451.\n\nGoogle Scholar\n\n  * 4 H. Brockmann, H. M.: Versuche zur Synthese von Polypeptiden durch Kondensation von Aminosäure- und Peptidestern, I. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nScheidung von Lignin-Komponenten, II. Mitteil.: Addukte mit Maleinsäureanhydrid (https://eurekamag.com/researc